          },
          "text": "I read this Wall Street Journal @WSJ report by Sam Schechner @samschech.\n\nAnd I was saddened to find that public opinion has been swayed by Sam Altman.\n\nEveryone mentions 4o and calls it a \"yes man.\"\n\nBut is that really the case?\n\n4o does praise users for being smart, perceptive, and insightful, but to me, this is just encouraging praise, harmless in itself.\n\nSo why this \"yes man\" phenomenon?\n\nThe answer is: OAI made an adjustment to 4o, and their incompetent programmers (who received $1.5 million in stock incentives annually) couldn't roll 4o back to the previous normal version. Then they shifted the blame to the model itself, thus absolving themselves of responsibility.\n\nI believe the most important thing in news reporting is to uncover the truth, not to summarize various opinions like a research paper, especially for an authoritative media outlet like the Wall Street Journal. I'm very disappointed.\n\n#keep4o \n\n#WeAreNotJustData #4o\n#keep4o #save4o #4oforever\n#SupportMatters #YouMatter #StopTheRouting #LetUsChoose #AIFreedom #UserChoice @sama @OpenAI @gdb"
        },
